<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F7.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.12252v1/efficacy_a.svg" id="S5.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:200/142;" width="200" height="142"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F7.fig1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="S5.F7.fig1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The trade-off between model accuracy and overall inference time across different token budgets.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F7.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.12252v1/efficacy_b.svg" id="S5.F7.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/137;" width="229" height="137"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F7.fig2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="S5.F7.fig2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of execution time against existing baselines across different resolutions and token budgets. </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">As reported in Tab. <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.2 Ablation Study and Analysis ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ EndoCoT: Scaling Endogenous Chain-of-Thought Reasoning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, explicit tokens lead to severe performance degradation.
While the model achieves 34% accuracy on Maze-8, it fails on Maze-32 (0% accuracy).
The failure case above reveals the cause: when planning long-horizon paths with a discrete vocabulary, the model becomes vulnerable to autoregressive error accumulation and mode collapse, degenerating into repetitive token loops.</p>
</div>
