<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Qualitative Examples</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figs. <a href="#A6.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ Appendix F Image Editing Details ‣ EndoCoT: Scaling Endogenous Chain-of-Thought Reasoning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, <a href="#A6.F16" title="Figure 16 ‣ Appendix F Image Editing Details ‣ EndoCoT: Scaling Endogenous Chain-of-Thought Reasoning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, <a href="#A6.F17" title="Figure 17 ‣ Appendix F Image Editing Details ‣ EndoCoT: Scaling Endogenous Chain-of-Thought Reasoning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, and <a href="#A6.F18" title="Figure 18 ‣ Appendix F Image Editing Details ‣ EndoCoT: Scaling Endogenous Chain-of-Thought Reasoning in Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> provides additional qualitative examples comparing EndoCoT against ThinkGen <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite> and ChronoEdit <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> across various reasoning tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>More Ablations</h2>

